      "id": "g11-03",
      "title": "Life experience with たことがある",
      "sourcePages": "260–261",
      "meaning": "Say that an event has occurred in your experience, or that it never has.",
      "formation": "Affirmative past short verb + ことがあります / ことがありません. Question: ことがありますか.",
      "notes": [
        "Negate あります for “never”; the verb before こと stays affirmative past.",
        "This reports experience, not a just-completed task. まだ〜ていません instead presents an expected task as pending.",
        "A short reply is あります/ありません. Do not reply with ことがあります by itself."
      ],
      "prerequisites": [
        "g09-01",
        "g04-01"
      ],
      "examples": [
        {
          "english": "I have been to Sapporo before.",
          "japanese": "札幌に行ったことがあります。",
          "kana": "さっぽろにいったことがあります。"
